WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.640
Welcome to my channel, I'm Pivokosa, you're you,

2
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:08.400
and today we're starting another new series called Fast Food at Home.

3
00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:13.430
My husband and I have been on a diet for two weeks and a sugar crisis hit,

4
00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:21.880
so we agreed to have one cheat meal a week, which I then came up with the idea of using for this series.

5
00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:34.160
For every fast food we make in this series, we'll look at whether it's faster to make at home or to order, whether it's cheaper, and whether it's tastier in the end.

6
00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:38.860
I don't think I'll be better than all the restaurants, absolutely not.

7
00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:44.790
I really love ordering in, and I like going to a restaurant too, but most of all I love ordering.

8
00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:52.210
So this competition isn't any kind of hate toward restaurants or ordering, it's not anti-ordering,

9
00:00:52.210 --> 00:01:01.200
but I think it can be made at home too and, given the astronomical prices, it may pay off a bit more for us, or maybe not.

10
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.980
That's what this series is for, to find out.

11
00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.910
Enough introduction, let's begin.

12
00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:10.520
For the first meal we're looking at my favourite pancake.

13
00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:15.480
I very rarely make pancakes at home, because you have to make a million.

14
00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:24.710
You can't make just one, you always end up with ten pancakes; instead of nicely eating one big pancake, I have to eat ten.

15
00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:27.120
I mean, I don't have to, but realistically I do.

16
00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:33.810
So I set myself the task of trying to change that, and that's what we'll do today.

17
00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:39.500
We'll make my favourite: euro krem, Plazma biscuits in milk, banana pancake,

18
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:43.080
and compare it with the pancake from Milki.

19
00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:47.980
We'll order the same one, weigh it at the end, and so on.

20
00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:51.780
Now let's race a little. First we'll order it through Wolt,

21
00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:56.580
and in the meantime, until it arrives, try to make one at home too.

22
00:01:56.740 --> 00:02:03.370
Here we are on Milki. I checked, the prices are quite similar on Wolt and in the restaurant, which is rare.

23
00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:09.540
Milki of course has their special creams and all that, we're certainly not going to compete with that,

24
00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:14.190
and for that it's absolutely worth ordering, they have those breaded ones and everything else.

25
00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:24.340
Absolutely lots of love for Milki, but let's see whether it really makes sense to pay 850 dinars for this ordinary pancake or whether we can make it at home too.

26
00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:29.340
Well, here we go, we have 20 to 30 minutes to make it, so let's get started quickly.

27
00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:32.060
I'll measure out 50 grams of flour.

28
00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:40.520
I bought most of the ingredients in these small packages, so it wouldn't be a case of "I have to spend a lot and then have leftovers",

29
00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:48.360
but I didn't do that only for the flour and the butter, because there's no smaller package, and most people use them anyway.

30
00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:56.130
To our flour we'll add hot water from the tap and a little milk.

31
00:02:56.130 --> 00:03:07.420
I'll put in a pinch of salt; some people put sugar in the batter too, but my mom doesn't, so I don't either.

32
00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:15.820
And now it feels strange to me: this is pancake batter, and it has sugar in it.

33
00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:27.990
And now we'll melt 20 grams of butter, and I'll pour part of it into this batter, and keep part for greasing the pan so the pancake doesn't stick.

34
00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:30.020
20 grams may be a lot.

35
00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:34.520
If we don't use it all... yes, 20 grams is really a lot.

36
00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.720
I'm turning into my mom.

37
00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:38.780
Now the batter, roughly.

38
00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:43.690
This butter can even be bought in a 10-gram pack, if you find it in your shop.

39
00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:48.550
Of course, I should have bought the normal 10-gram pack, but right here where I live there wasn't any.

40
00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:49.880
But we'll count the price of it.

41
00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:52.960
While that melts, we'll prepare our Plazma.

42
00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:57.420
I mean, I didn't want to take the whole big pack of ground Plazma, so there wouldn't be any extra.

43
00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:01.470
So I took this smallest pack, which we'll now grind.

44
00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:06.500
And if there isn't enough, I have more ground Plazma at home, and we'll include it at the end.

45
00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:09.990
There, our butter has melted.

46
00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:20.190
Now I'll pour part into our batter, part into a little bowl for extra greasing, and part can stay in the pan.

47
00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:24.040
There, we'll set our batter aside.

48
00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:34.490
The Plazma can be ground of course with a pestle, a spoon, a fork, additionally with milk, but...

49
00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:40.290
Come on, since we have a blender anyway, let's use it a bit.

50
00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:43.860
We'll put all the Plazma inside.

51
00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:46.090
Here's our Plazma.

52
00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:52.270
Now we'll pour our milk into the Plazma.

53
00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:58.050
For the price of milk I'll use the half-litre one from Imlek,

54
00:04:58.050 --> 00:05:07.260
but I use farm milk myself and I recommend that everyone buy from the ethical list of dairies,

55
00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:10.470
if you're able to, of course.

56
00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:19.100
A consistency like this, I like it, but it seems to me there'll be too little.

57
00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:23.480
Now we'll see how much I'll manage to roll into our pancake.

58
00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:29.670
Basically, we're ready now. In fact, we used 200 ml of milk, in total.

59
00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:34.740
Now we'll see whether this will be enough for us, I'm not sure.

60
00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:38.260
I can estimate whether this is one pancake or two.

61
00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:43.740
Basically, this pancake batter would benefit from resting a bit, at least half an hour,

62
00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:46.810
but we're racing today, so we don't have time.

63
00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:52.760
We've prepared all our ingredients: the Plazma... I haven't sliced the banana yet, we can do that on the spot.

64
00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:55.470
Now we'll heat our pan and bake.

65
00:05:55.470 --> 00:06:03.820
My big problem with making pancakes at home is that I don't have that hot plate that they have in pancake places,

66
00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:11.390
so the pancake isn't that big, but this is the biggest pan I have, so we'll try in it.

67
00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:15.830
Well, even if we make two small ones, we'll somehow get by.

68
00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:20.440
You know how they say: the first pancake gets thrown away, but not with us.

69
00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:23.870
Not this time. And normally I don't throw it away.

70
00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:27.970
I'll pour on some more of this butter, so it's minimally greasy.

71
00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:33.960
And I normally do this part with a ladle, but this time I don't even know whether it could scoop it up,

72
00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.750
so we'll pour straight from the container.

73
00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:50.630
Well, one pancake. One and a short one, maybe it will turn out as two.

74
00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:58.370
When the pancake batter has an egg, of course it's nicer, tastier, but it isn't necessary.

75
00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:11.880
We found that out when my mom was filming Lenten pancakes for her channel and made beautiful pancakes only from flour and warm water, literally without milk and, of course, without butter.

76
00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:16.890
They were great, so now we'll try to recreate that.

77
00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:18.580
The small one tore, it's not ideal.

78
00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:23.830
And we'll load it up with so much of this sweet stuff that I think the difference won't really be noticeable.

79
00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:29.420
Wolt has already arrived.

80
00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:35.490
Honestly, I thought it would take them a bit longer, but no.

81
00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:41.570
There's no chance of keeping up with this pan, it all happened in two minutes.

82
00:07:41.570 --> 00:07:47.600
Milki has arrived, as you heard, so we lost the battle for time, but not the war.

83
00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:51.180
We lost this time too, and next time we'll be faster.

84
00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:57.340
And we found out that you can't make pancakes on this pan, because it started to stick,

85
00:07:57.340 --> 00:08:02.110
and in the meantime I tried to make one on the metal one too and that didn't work.

86
00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:05.770
So we'll simply have to use the small pan.

87
00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:14.560
Don't worry, it will absolutely get eaten, like a Kaiserschmarrn in our version, and we'll bake several smaller pancakes.

88
00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:18.510
What can we do? If I had a bigger pan it would be great,

89
00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:24.170
but this is more of a standard pancake pan, the kind most households have.

90
00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:28.280
Now we'll whisk up a new batter.

91
00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:40.600
This time I'll put in an egg, because it seemed to me that with that pan it didn't really suit it that there was no egg.

92
00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:52.810
We'll put in one egg and about 50 ml of milk to start, a little salt and now enough flour to thicken it.

93
00:08:52.810 --> 00:08:57.430
A bit more, that's 70, 80,

94
00:08:57.430 --> 00:09:05.470
and now some water, warm from the tap, to thin it out.

95
00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:09.850
This batter would again benefit from resting, of course, but we're still racing.

96
00:09:09.850 --> 00:09:13.580
We lost badly, we're trying to get the best time we can.

97
00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:17.250
I'll also pour the bit of butter that we counted straight into the batter.

98
00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:23.900
You can already see how much nicer the batter is, even if I poured too much and poured some off.

99
00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:26.790
It's simply much better with an egg.

100
00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:32.210
I don't know how my mom magically managed to make those Lenten ones.

101
00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:37.200
Maybe the trick was that there was oil instead of butter, who knows,

102
00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:41.140
or maybe the trick was that it's still mama Buba.

103
00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:49.550
Here are our little pancakes. The first isn't quite ultra-perfect, but considering we made it in such a rush...

104
00:09:49.550 --> 00:09:55.580
Each next one will go more easily, because the batter is more and more rested, the pan hotter and hotter,

105
00:09:55.580 --> 00:09:58.260
so see you when we've baked them all.

106
00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:01.140
There, we've made our pancakes.

107
00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:09.000
We made six of these smaller pancakes, and this bit at the end that was left over wasn't really enough for a whole one.

108
00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:15.380
Well, now we'll see whether we'll make six smaller pancakes or what we'll do.

109
00:10:17.830 --> 00:10:23.770
We'll open it to see how Milki arrived.

110
00:10:23.770 --> 00:10:29.260
This really isn't sponsored. God.

111
00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:36.220
This is literally the size of my head. It looks really big, it looks nice.

112
00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:42.240
Of course, how else would it look, right? It looks like there's really a lot of euro krem.

113
00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:48.180
And now, that triangle of hers is about the size of one of my pancakes,

114
00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:57.810
so it occurred to me to construct one huge one from these six, so that we don't give up as far as that size goes.

115
00:10:57.810 --> 00:11:01.740
It's not the same when it's six small ones and when it's that big one,

116
00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:04.920
now we'll try to recreate it.

117
00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:07.360
Mother of God, Jesus Christ.

118
00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:16.110
Oh, my mom's beautiful flowers, I should thank my mother for growing them so nicely and for giving them to me.

119
00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:23.180
We'll just move them out of the frame a bit to try to make this madness of ours.

120
00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:25.560
In the end our pancakes turned out nice.

121
00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:29.120
I'm satisfied, even though they didn't rest, they're really not bad.

122
00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:38.290
There. And in the centre we can put our sixth one,

123
00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:45.900
and now we'll spread our little flower with euro krem and Plazma and add the banana.

124
00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:55.690
A definite advantage of making it at home is that you can spread as much as you like.

125
00:11:55.690 --> 00:12:04.930
Maybe it's not really an advantage for your health, but it's a definite advantage for taste,

126
00:12:04.930 --> 00:12:10.610
and you can make sure every little bit is spread.

127
00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:18.180
Now I'll spread here and in between. 200 grams of euro krem will go onto this pancake.

128
00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:24.490
Our euro krem flower is spread. Now we'll add all of our Plazma.

129
00:12:26.190 --> 00:12:31.540
Now, I'm not sure whether they put it on just one part or spread it over the whole thing.

130
00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:36.310
But I'll decide that this little triangle is where the Plazma will go.

131
00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:37.670
And more banana.

132
00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:45.270
Lately I eat it with peanuts and coconut, but okay, that was a bit too much for this video.

133
00:12:45.670 --> 00:12:49.150
This is my standard, and the rest is too much for me.

134
00:12:49.150 --> 00:12:55.150
And however many of those there are in pancake places, with coconut milk, pistachios, this, that, crazy pancakes,

135
00:12:55.150 --> 00:13:01.400
somehow I don't feel like I've had pancakes unless I eat one with euro krem, Plazma, milk and banana.

136
00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:08.760
I mean, it's like when you order a pizza, you have to get a Capricciosa, and then one more thing to try, right?

137
00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:13.140
It can't go without a Capricciosa, so I can't do a pancake without this one.

138
00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:17.590
I have to eat this one, and then I can try all the others.

139
00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:21.930
Now, God help me, so you can see it better.

140
00:13:21.930 --> 00:13:26.730
The way I imagined it, well, I didn't quite imagine it like this.

141
00:13:26.730 --> 00:13:32.600
I think they fold it in half, like, we pretend it's a circle.

142
00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:39.070
This is how much euro krem we have left, we'll count it as if we used it all.

143
00:13:39.070 --> 00:13:47.490
And then it's like this and like this, right? I wrap it up. A bit better, but we can't do any better than that.

144
00:13:48.410 --> 00:13:51.790
We'll move it onto our plate.

145
00:13:51.790 --> 00:14:03.020
Now that we've finished, what's left is to weigh them, to see how much we got here and how much there.

146
00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:15.230
I'll also move the ordered one onto the same plate. I tared it, so we'll calculate exactly how much each one weighs.

147
00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:20.250
Theirs is 560 grams, hats off, and ours is 706.

148
00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:24.500
Like this, I don't know if you can see: 706 and 560.

149
00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:29.570
So, as far as time goes, fast food gets 1 point.

150
00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:35.250
As far as size goes, we get 1 point, so we're now at 1:1.

151
00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:44.320
As far as visual identity and presentation go, I think we can agree that fast food gets 1 point.

152
00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:50.940
I'm fine with that, ours is cute and homemade, but this one is just how it should be.

153
00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:52.470
So that's 2:1.

154
00:14:52.470 --> 00:15:09.680
As for price, it's a bit cheaper to make this bigger one and you still have a few ingredients left for other things, especially when you take delivery into account, but even without delivery it's simply cheaper to make at home.

155
00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:18.160
So we get a point there. 2:2 officially, and what's left is the deciding vote: which one is tastier.

156
00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:29.350
You know what? I just remembered, while packing it up, that I can also warm up the euro krem and pour it over just as nicely as they do.

157
00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:31.340
I hope so. Or maybe not quite.

158
00:15:31.340 --> 00:15:38.550
Okay, it's better, but I think the point for visual identity still stays with them.

159
00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:42.660
Now we'll taste. First we'll try theirs.

160
00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:46.040
Here it is. There's a pile of layers there, pancakes.

161
00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:50.810
There's filling too, with euro krem and Plazma in milk. No mistake.

162
00:15:50.810 --> 00:16:00.610
You see it has everything. The only thing is I think that they generally, pancake places, when they spread euro krem, they don't spread pure euro krem.

163
00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:08.820
First of all, we saw how hard it is to spread, and at the same time I think it simply wouldn't pay off for them.

164
00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:15.710
Because the extra charge is usually around 100 to 200 dinars, and this little tub costs 200-something.

165
00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:18.820
And now let's try our monster.

166
00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:24.780
I normally like to eat pancakes with my hands, but for that I need that holder of theirs.

167
00:16:24.780 --> 00:16:30.970
They struggle with them too, with these big ones, of course. They simply have to use a fork and knife.

168
00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:34.390
Juicy, juicy.

169
00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:38.630
Come on, let me see. It's a different taste.

170
00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:49.470
I don't know what it's down to, the taste of the euro krem is definitely different, which means they surely dilute it with something.

171
00:16:49.470 --> 00:16:53.600
But I like these more when they're a bit thinner.

172
00:16:53.600 --> 00:17:09.260
Their pancakes are quite a bit thicker, which is of course necessary to hold all the ingredients they offer, so you don't struggle like this, but I think we win on taste, because this portion is still a little too big for one person,

173
00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:17.970
for two people it's just right. My husband and I will split it, and it will be just enough to hold out until next week and the next cheating on the diet.

174
00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:27.540
Of course, you can make something smaller and more normal, but I simply had to see whether I could make this at home as if I had ordered it.

175
00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:32.370
And I think we succeeded, with a bit of trouble, of course.

176
00:17:32.370 --> 00:17:41.200
I think we would even have been somewhere near on time if I hadn't had these mishaps in the kitchen,

177
00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:45.300
but I think this was completely successful for us.

178
00:17:45.300 --> 00:17:48.600
And honestly, I'd rather eat this homemade one.

179
00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:52.170
It has that familiar taste of euro krem and Plazma.

180
00:17:52.170 --> 00:18:01.040
I don't know, I have to try, I don't know why it's so different, whether it's because of the amount or something there...

181
00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:10.800
Still, I have nothing against Milki, I love Milki, of course, everyone in business has to change something.

182
00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:17.450
Yes, you see how that euro krem is runnier, I think that's...

183
00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:25.100
It's definitely different, and much, much more pancake and less of all this.

184
00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:27.230
Look at this mess of mine here,

185
00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:30.270
someone may judge me, but definitely not me. All in all,

186
00:18:30.270 --> 00:18:35.680
one successful shoot, I hope you'll like this series, so I can film more.

187
00:18:35.680 --> 00:18:45.930
Like the video, comment so I know you like it, and we plan to go back for good to our regular slot, Sundays at half past ten in the morning.

188
00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:57.700
For those who don't like this series and miss Grandma, I'm planning another series not related to cooking, with Grandma, which you'll most likely watch next week.

189
00:18:57.700 --> 00:19:03.810
Thank you so much for watching, love each other, take care of yourselves and, as always, stay chubby.

190
00:19:03.810 --> 00:19:04.100
Bye!
